{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea","id":460556,"title":"So We're Gonna See Pangaea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-28T18:24:25-07:00","id":460556,"title":"So We're Gonna See Pangaea","content":"DaveB has told us that the Neolithic setting in Dark Eras takes place before the Sundering. So, we'll be seeing Pangaea or at least something like it.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T18:32:41-07:00","id":460582,"title":"","content":"If anyone hears erratic, girlish shrieking from somewhere far away, it's just me.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I have been waiting for this moment for a long, long time. It's been hinted at that the tribes were founded during the times of prehistoric humanity, so if I'm right, this means that the werewolves seeking out the Firstborn didn't happen long after the fall of the Border Marches.<br /> <br /> Seriously, seriously pumped for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T18:32:55-07:00","id":460583,"title":"","content":"To manage your expectations, you should read the second edition version of the Sundering myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T18:35:43-07:00","id":460585,"title":"","content":"I like it as a setting to make use of, but like many fantastic historic kinds of settings I have a hard time imagining I'll ever use it as the BASE location for a game. More like I would use it for a back story or for a strange plot twist to visit the locale temporarily. WoD in the &quot;somewhere around now&quot; is what I'll always go back to.<br /> <br /> Still I like it. It seems like it will have an &quot;Age of Legends&quot; feel. Would have preferred pirates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom"