lass=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=461503#post461503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My anthropology bachelor is itching for this harder now. Neolithic Mage sounded intriguing, Neolithic werewolf makes me happy in an almost perverse way.<br /> <br /> And what the what? Vampire originated from strix possessed corpses? I thought that was just a rumor! Or are there multiple origins for the vamps?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are more origin stories for vampires than there are Clans to have them. It's part of the beauty of Requiem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:05:38-07:00","id":461547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=461504#post461504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are more origin stories for vampires than there are Clans to have them. It's part of the beauty of Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b><a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/83024157855/they-say-there-are-many-unique-curses-theres\" target=\"_blank\">so many teeth</a></b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:30:23-07:00","id":461631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=461485#post461485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe...<br /> <br /> Anpu hasn't really been fleshed out in the Mummy line and honestly I see his personality being mostly focused running Duat and being sympathetic to the Arisen. After all, they got screwed by the Shan'iatu as much as he was. Given if the conversation in the intro is correct on that part, then he's been mostly screaming &quot;WTF!&quot; and &quot;You had one job! One job!&quot; to the Shan'iatu while attempting to clean up their mess as his role will allow.<br /> <br /> Considering how major the Rite of Return was, I wouldn't be surprised if Duat was some kind of oasis paradise before the Shan'iatu screwed that up and made it a wasteland of their own devising and Anpu being pissed as hell because he's now having to clean that shit up and knows how futile it is to sweep sand out of a desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how that relates to potential territorial disputes between him and Mother Wolf, particularly over, say, geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:52:13-07:00","id":461646,"title":"","content":"This kind of history is out of my wheelhouse, but does it seem to anyone else like Father Wolf may have become weakened, at least in part, due to humanity depending less on hunting during the Neolithic, as farming and agriculture began?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:53:30-07:00","id":461648,"title":"","content":"That might have been a major factor, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T17:14:10-07:00","id":461658,"title":"","content":"It actually does make a tremendous amount of sense. If one of the resonances Father Wolf fed from was Hunting, and it probably was, he would logically be weakened by finding less of it due to the development of human cultures into sedentism and establishing of agriculture-reliant settlements.<br /> <br /> And with the some of the foes he hunted at the time... he needed that essence to keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T17:23:34-07:00","id":461667,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that agriculture means unprecedented numbers of humans pouring their emotional resonance into single locations for extended periods of time. Spirits that <i>Urfarah</i> hasn't normally had trouble with are now being given a chance to spawn and grow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T20:27:38-07:00","id":461813,"title":"","content":"Birth of agriculture as the sundering is looking better with each passing comment. Not only that, but it also adds to the Sumerian language being linguistically similar to the first tongue. I often wondered how the two languages were similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T20:41:42-07:00","id":461817,"title":"","content":"Well there would still be steps between, of course. Father Wolf weakens as humanity turns from some of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persistence_hunting\" target=\"_blank\">greatest hunters</a> to farmers.<br /> <br /> In a way, it even fits with the Firstborn. Sagrim-Ur always wanted to know what would happen if everything changed drastically, and in at least one of his origin stories acted to take 'special care to look after them.' Death Wolf, another survivor, spoke of death saying, 'One only need not be afraid of changing.' But Father Wolf has been presented as a static, though multifaceted being.<br /> <br /> And Huzuruth-Ur, who hates the Forsaken for taking Pangaea away, making his tribe dishonor the works of man and focusing them on the sacred prey of those who dishonor the hunt. With his hateful and vengeful attitude it seems to fit with humanity and not-hunting having a fault in the collapse of Pangaea.<br /> <br /> Getting a little out there here, but considering the importance of the hunt in the development of humanity and your thoughts on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endurance_running_hypothesis\" target=\"_blank\">certain theories</a>, perhaps the reason there's no humanity spirits is because long ago, the First Pack killed him. If the name of things like Father's Form is accurate and Urfarah wasn't confined to the form of a wolf but could shift like the Uratha, perhaps Luna wouldn't have needed to turn into a human in order to help create werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2015, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:25:04-07:00","id":462180,"title":"","content":"One of the most interesting things that we'll be exploring in this chapter, for me, is the nature of the Border Marches, and how that affects the lives of Awakened and Uratha alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:22:53-07:00","id":462216,"title":"","content":"It will certainly be very interesting. I've always been curious why people who weren't sorcerers or spiritualists would try to visit the Hisil.<br /> <br /> And of course, what the Border Marches actually are. We were discussing it in one of Xenu's Paradox' threads and it seems to be some sort of passageway between worlds, like the Hedge, so it'll be neat to see if that pans out or not. Plus a place of strange kingdoms and Plague Kings and Spinner Hags is bound to be intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:40:54-07:00","id":462377,"title":"","content":"Does it make me a terrible person if I kind of want it to be like the world during the time of Avatar Wan in that two-part episode from the Legend of Korra?<br /> <br /> (Relevant links if you have no idea what I'm talking about and want to watch:<br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Do not post links to pirated material.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-30-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T08:27:38-07:00","id":561953,"title":"","content":"There's some news, and I love it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-end-is-the-beginning-is-the-end-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-end-is-the-beginning-is-the-end-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> The End is the Beginning is the End [Mage: The Awakening] [Dark Eras] [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-end-is-the-beginning-is-the-end-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-end-is-the-beginning-is-the-end-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAN