nyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only a minor one, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:17:51-07:00","id":561991,"title":"","content":"One word: Pangaens. Native beings of the Border Marches that were not inherently ephemeral. <i>Father Wolf was a pangaen.</i><br /> <br /> WHICH EXPLAINS A LOT. Like how he could have physical offspring with Luna, for one.<br /> <br /> Also this... kind of makes it even more understandable how the Uratha of the time that would become the Pure were so pissed off. What with <i>their native land</i> <i>being crushed into the Gauntlet.</i> The Pure literally lost their homelands. <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(So did the Forsaken, but 'they're race traitors so what's your point?')</span><br /> <br /> <br /> I love what we're seeing of the Werewolf Neolithic crossover material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:17:36-07:00","id":562065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=561991#post561991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also this... kind of makes it even more understandable how the Uratha of the time that would become the Pure were so pissed off. What with <i>their native land</i> <i>being crushed into the Gauntlet.</i> The Pure literally lost their homelands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does mention that The Wolf was weakening, losing his grip on the border. <i>Maybe</i> the Uratha realized that unless they did something the spirit world was going to run roughshod over the material and <i>deliberately</i> sacrificed pangaea in order to slam the door shut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:29:59-07:00","id":562073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=562065#post562065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does mention that The Wolf was weakening, losing his grip on the border. <i>Maybe</i> the Uratha realized that unless they did something the spirit world was going to run roughshod over the material and <i>deliberately</i> sacrificed pangaea in order to slam the door shut.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a really interesting take on it. I like that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:05:29-07:00","id":562090,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty cool twist, and one that would only compound the conflict between the original Pure and the Forsaken at that. I kinda like it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:21:13-07:00","id":562106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=562065#post562065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does mention that The Wolf was weakening, losing his grip on the border. <i>Maybe</i> the Uratha realized that unless they did something the spirit world was going to run roughshod over the material and <i>deliberately</i> sacrificed pangaea in order to slam the door shut.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Hasn't that <i>always</i> been the reasoning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:28:55-07:00","id":562109,"title":"","content":"Replace Father Wolf so that the spirit world wouldn't run roughshod over the material yeah, but I'm not sure the whole &quot;devastate the Border Marches and erect the Gauntlet in their place to separate the worlds&quot; part was planned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:48:19-07:00","id":562114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=562106#post562106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Hasn't that <i>always</i> been the reasoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but there's subtle differences here. For one, Werewolves are apparently heavily established and spread out, not one pack with Father wolf at the head. Secondly, apparently the rate of spiritual incursion into the material is pretty damn bad. Past the point where something as simple as taking his place wouldn't have helped. Especially since the source of his power itself was waning. Father Wolf <i>as</i> <i>a</i><i> concept</i> was beginning to fade.<br /> <br /> Maybe the bordermarches were already doomed, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:15:11-07:00","id":562126,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a pretty subtle difference; the end-goal is certainly the same (protect the flesh from the encroaching spirit), as are the methods (kill Wolf). But there's a definite difference in intention between &quot;kill Wolf so we can take his place as warden(s) of the Border Marches&quot; versus &quot;kill Wolf so there won't be Border Marches any more.&quot; It makes the loss of Pangea a calculated tacticial sacrifice instead of an unintended consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:26:25-07:00","id":562128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=461646#post461646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of history is out of my wheelhouse, but does it seem to anyone else like Father Wolf may have become weakened, at least in part, due to humanity depending less on hunting during the Neolithic, as farming and agriculture began?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that guess was <i>on point!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:48:27-07:00","id":562136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=562128#post562128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn, that guess was <i>on point!</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it was a very good guess.<br /> <br /> Humans really are perfect killing machines, evolution-wise, and looking at it from an evolutionary psychology point of view, the development of agriculture was a collosal mistake. Sure, far more of us could survive doing it, and it kicked our population up from the &quot;one major tectonic event from extinction&quot; level it yoyoed into since our ancestors learned how to run long-distance, but the quality of life is <i>terrible</i>. There's been studies done on how many hours a day it takes to support an adult human with a child through hunting versus through agriculture. Essentially, everyone made their lives a whole lot worse in order that a whole lot more of them could live.<br /> <br /> And people say socialism doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:48:47-07:00","id":562138,"title":"","content":"So the Uratha in this era don't have a unified approach about<i> Urfarah's</i> decline, not even something as straightforward as a split mirroring Pure and Forsaken. There are a lot of different beliefs and philosophies about what to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:38:06-07:00","id":562236,"title":"","content":"As a fan of best firstborn, I must ask, did the Bale Hounds exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:05:55-07:00","id":562243,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned over in the Mummy forum, I'm really excited to see Brine Born as a major fixture in this era rather than a footnote. The importance of the fish shifters to ancient Sumerian mythology shouldn't be overlooked in favor of wolf-centric viewpoints which Sumerians did not, in actuality, have to anywhere near such a severe degree. It'd be very interesting to see the 'fall' of this race.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:30:48-07:00","id":562276,"title":"","content":"The culture we're focusing on, the Vinca, aren't on the coast; while the earliest settlements of what will one day become Sumer are occurring during the time period of the chapter, the city of Uruk won't even exist for over a millennia yet.<br /> <br /> Now I'd be happy to write a fish-sages expansion for the Neolithic chapter if a backer were to have bought in to add another 5k words for it or whatnot, but sadly that isn't the case so you'll mostly have to be content with what hints I put into the Werewolf 2e corebook for now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link"