\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-21-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:45:51-07:00","id":563108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563087#post563087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't Jnanamukti the cult of Magi within the Mysterium that wished to return mankind to the Bronze Ages? The Heresy that wanted to remove all post-Atlantean technology? Or am I thinking of another?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the Jnanamukti are the darshana, or shool or philosophy, from the To The Strongest setting that style themselves as the school of wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:58:49-07:00","id":563115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563108#post563108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, the Jnanamukti are the darshana, or shool or philosophy, from the To The Strongest setting that style themselves as the school of wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. On p.81 of the Mysterium they are shown as a modern-day heresy among the Mysterium. They believe that sleeper society and technology, along with other supernatural entities push the fallen away from the Supernal, and therefore need to be destroyed. They, alongside the Daksha legacy supported the Nazis during WW2, the Daksha did it because they agreed with their ideas, while the Jnanamukti wanted a war that could destroy mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:38:21-07:00","id":563296,"title":"","content":"Considering the number of Apocalyptic scenarios, it wouldn't be -that- hard to bring back the world to Pangaean times. But it looks like Pangaea itself might require something else to bring it back.<br /> <br /> Either way, the God Machine seems like the weak point in any attempt to stop the Predator Kings. While it would be hard to destroy every agricultural center in the world, at least without the help of the beshilu or Fire-Touched, the God Machine has a bundle of apocalypses ready to go in Seattle. They already have a representative in every pack in Seattle, they're just being sort of manipulated by the Fang Prophet. As an added bonus, the God Machine might have a timeline where Pangaea didn't disappear at all stashed somewhere.<br /> <br /> Off hand, I'd theorize that the firstborn aren't pure spirit. Which might explain their relative strength when wolf populations are so low, even with their multiple Influences and the service of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:48:38-07:00","id":563307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563108#post563108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, the Jnanamukti are the darshana, or shool or philosophy, from the To The Strongest setting that style themselves as the school of wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Close - the Hellenistic forbears of the Mysterium are the <b>Jnanashakti. </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:53:16-07:00","id":563310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563296#post563296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the number of Apocalyptic scenarios, it wouldn't be -that- hard to bring back the world to Pangaean times. But it looks like Pangaea itself might require something else to bring it back.<br /> <br /> Either way, the God Machine seems like the weak point in any attempt to stop the Predator Kings. While it would be hard to destroy every agricultural center in the world, at least without the help of the beshilu or Fire-Touched, the God Machine has a bundle of apocalypses ready to go in Seattle. They already have a representative in every pack in Seattle, they're just being sort of manipulated by the Fang Prophet. As an added bonus, the God Machine might have a timeline where Pangaea didn't disappear at all stashed somewhere.<br /> <br /> Off hand, I'd theorize that the firstborn aren't pure spirit. Which might explain their relative strength when wolf populations are so low, even with their multiple Influences and the service of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the God Machine really so widespread and deeply embedded that it has agents and followers in every werewolf pack and vampire court, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:59:33-07:00","id":563315,"title":"","content":"Ah, I meant the Predator Kings have a representative in every Pure pack in Seattle. As for whether or not the God Machine has agents in every supernatural microcosm, it doesn't seem likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2015, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:25:39-07:00","id":563361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=562872#post562872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember the exact wording I used off-hand, but perhaps this will shed some light on the inferences about the Predator King sacred hunts in 2e <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do... do their Sacred Hunts allow them to travel through the Gauntlet as thought it was the Border Marches again, more easily moving between the Shadow and the physical?<br /> <br /> Because that's starting to sound eerily likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:16:06-07:00","id":563400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563310#post563310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the God Machine really so widespread and deeply embedded that it has agents and followers in every werewolf pack and vampire court, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have it that way in my game, though I will say in my nwod games, the God-Machine is itself a fairly embedded part of what makes reality function now. I think though outside of Angels sent to do specific Missions and they're sent to poke the supernaturals if a specific Infrastructure/Occult Matrix needs to be created, the supernatural communities are the same as humanity and pretty much another bunch of little pawns for whatever the bigger picture may be, which is beyond scope for any game I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:28:55-07:00","id":563413,"title":"","content":"I think it's more like &quot;remember that random extra that meant your werewolf chose a different back alley to transform in? Angel.&quot;<br /> <br /> We're talking really subtle things that most of the time you just wouldn't notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:14:31-07:00","id":563437,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can get behind that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally have the God-Machine involved in responsibility for Pangaea's shift into The Gauntlet, though I could possibly be sold on the idea of it causing occult matrix in order to keep The Gauntlet up. <i>Why</i> it is stopping the regeneration of Pangaea is something else entirely, though I'd like to think in some way specific Infrastructure is in place to make sure Spirits can cross over, as there are cogs in the Shadow and it has some use for Spirits in what it does, given the vibe got from it so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:01:34-07:00","id":563467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563307#post563307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Close - the Hellenistic forbears of the Mysterium are the <b>Jnanashakti. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Gah, right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:28:26-07:00","id":563605,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this means that some of the Places That Aren't aren't places lacking a reflection in the real world, but artifacts of Pangaea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=563437#post563437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't personally have the God-Machine involved in responsibility for Pangaea's shift into The Gauntlet</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't implying that. I'm still of the mind that it was Father Wolf's death, along with perhaps Luna's retribution.<br /> <br /> But as of the Splintered City: Seattle book, the God Machine has a sort of container called the Apocalypse Vault where it has stashed would-be events that would end the world, if the possible futures hadn't been snipped off ahead of time. If the God Machine has alternate futures, it may have one where whatever happened to Pangaea didn't happen.<br /> <br /> So it wasn't that the God Machine had a hand in anything or would help or hinder. But wiping out all of humanity or altering the world to such a degree that it fits Pangaea is something that would be difficult, particularly considering as someone pointed out above, most of the other supernaturals would be fervently against it. But if all it takes is to find the Apocalypse Vault and pop it open, the Predator Kings have a much easier job, even considering the defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T22:30:00-07:00","id":563738,"title":"","content":"It begs the question if Gauru form is going to work similarly to how it worked in the <i>Wolves of Bau, </i>or alternatively if all start with Father's Form, or if they are changing that. I think that it makes more sense for Werewolves, themselves, to be fundamentally more, and with Father's Form facet, it makes sense for a more free use of Gauru form to be the way to show this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T18:03:58-07:00","id":565907,"title":"","content":"Would Ferals from Changing Breeds be Pangians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:41:06-07:00","id":567023,"title":"","content":"They could well be. I believe there is mention of other shape changers. More importantly we have potential insight into the creatures that existed in the border marches. Is it still just a thin dimension or was it it's own shadow realm before the shadow? Something like the pnumbra to the deep umbra in apocalypse? If that's the case then the forsaken are guilty of quite a lot of spiritual genocide with father wolf's death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:23:30-07:00","id":567064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=565907#post565907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Ferals from Changing Breeds be Pangians?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read Changing Breeds; if any of the shapeshifter types from there have their origins tied in with the sorts of divinities that Father Wolf hunted then yes, they might be descended from Pangaeans. Otherwise, probably not. Changing Breeds aren't part of the Mage or Werewolf lines so I haven't addressed them in the chapter text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:07:37-07:00","id":568654,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, no, the changing breeds aren't known for being descended from deities, they're fluff is that they're Gaia's immune response against humanity's depredation ala wta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:29:22-07:00","id":568670,"title":"","content":"I believe that's a theory someone in the Slasher book throws around about them, too, that they are humanity's defense mechanism against the supernaturals. The white cell theory is an interesting one, in either case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:15:51-07:00","id":568746,"title":"","content":"Slasher is a book I need to buy at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:10:57-07:00","id":569048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=568670#post568670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that's a theory someone in the Slasher book throws around about them, too, that they are humanity's defense mechanism against the supernaturals. The white cell theory is an interesting one, in either case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically.. a cross between Heroes and Beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:15:30-07:00","id":569051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=568654#post568654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If memory serves, no, the changing breeds aren't known for being descended from deities, they're fluff is that they're Gaia's immune response against humanity's depredation ala wta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so in that case Changing Breeds probably don't have anything to do with Pangaea.<br /> <br /> Some other shapeshifters, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T00:44:52-07:00","id":570022,"title":"","content":"Yes, pangea might very well have been the origin for some shapeshifters from War Against the Pure- the fish guys were already mentioned I believe, the cats and the cockroaches could be remnants of Pangea too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:00:00-07:00","id":570316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460556-so-we-re-gonna-see-pangaea?p=568746#post568746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slasher is a book I need to buy at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a really nice book, but World of Darkness has pretty much killed it when it comes to antagonist books.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's mostly for Storytellers, or players of Slashers, but it does have a new Hunter Conspiracy, VASCU. Who are sort of like psychic Profiler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T20:33:56-07:00","id":572127,"title":"","content":"One of the neat things about the Slashers book is that it points out how easy it is for Hunters to turn into Slashers. One piece of fiction from the book involves a scientifically-minded Hunter who took down some kind of witch, but is now convinced that the witch's magic inflicted some kind of contamination that continues to put people at risk. He proceeded to track down and murder everyone he could find who had been touched by the witch's magic, seal them up in barrels of rock salt, and perform some kind of psudo-sciencey procedure that he believed would safely extract and contain the contaminant. In the end, he's taken down by another Hunter, protesting all the while that he's one of the good guys.<br /> <br /> It also implies that Slashers are, in some sense, a fundamental part of humanity. As I recall, one theory is that, at some point in the distant past, humanity's survival was dependent on terrifying killing machines resembling present-day Slashers. This ties in nicely with the Neolithic Chapter's emphasis on humanity's role as the ultimate hunters (at least in the world of flesh) prior to the beginning of agriculture. In the real world, human beings were able to take down all sorts of dangerous animals thanks mostly to our complex mode of communication, our cooperative problem solving abilities, and our advanced tool use. In the World of Darkness, maybe humans had a little something more than that which made them the scariest predators in a wold riddled with supernatural terrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-28-2015, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}